\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 2. Top three behavioural risks to monitor\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Risk 1: Acting before fully checking consequences\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 This is the most prominent reflective signal in the profile. It does not establish harmful behaviour, but it supports monitoring how you make decisions under pressure.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Observable behaviours might include:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Making an irreversible decision without a short review.\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Bypassing a process because the outcome seems obviously desirable.\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Sending a blunt message while frustrated.\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Discounting second-order effects on morale, trust, reputation, or workload.\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Treating caution from others as resistance rather than useful risk information.\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Assuming that harm can be repaired later if the decision succeeds.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Safeguard:
\f0\b0  Introduce a deliberate pause for decisions that are high-impact, difficult to reverse, emotionally charged, or consequential for someone with less power.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Risk 2: Using information or influence too selectively\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 Strategic communication is not inherently problematic. The risk arises when persuasion becomes insufficiently transparent or when information asymmetry is used primarily to secure a preferred outcome.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Observable behaviours might include:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Presenting only the evidence supporting your preferred option.\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Giving different stakeholders materially different explanations.\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Consulting people after the practical decision has already been made.\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Withholding relevant constraints because disclosure might weaken support.\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Framing choices so that one option appears inevitable.\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Building informal agreement before affected parties can participate meaningfully.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Safeguard:
\f0\b0  Ask what a reasonable stakeholder would need to know to understand the decision, its trade-offs, and your own interests.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

