\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 Empathy at 61 is an emerging capacity, not an absence of empathy. It may already be available but less consistent when you are hurried, frustrated, or strongly focused on an outcome.\
Empathy does not require agreeing with everyone or avoiding difficult decisions. It means accurately considering how the situation appears from another person's position and incorporating foreseeable human impact.\
It can regulate risk by helping you:\
