\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 5. Short workplace scripts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Seeking feedback\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93I\'92m working on how I make decisions under pressure. Thinking about the last few weeks, what is one behaviour I should continue and one I should adjust?\'94\
For someone who may be cautious about disagreeing:\
\'93You do not need to comment on my intentions or personality. I\'92m looking for one specific behaviour that made it easier or harder to work with me.\'94\
When receiving difficult feedback:\
\'93Thank you. I\'92m going to reflect before responding. Could you give me one example so I can understand the behaviour and its impact?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Pausing before a reactive decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93I have a strong initial reaction, so I do not want to make the final decision in that state. I\'92m going to check the consequences and come back by [time].\'94\
For a meeting:\
\'93Before we commit, I want to test who could be adversely affected, what we may be missing, and whether there is a reversible first step.\'94\
For an email or message:\
\'93I have drafted a response, but I\'92m holding it until I can review the tone, evidence, and likely impact.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Giving credit\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93I want to be explicit that [name/team] developed the core idea and did the work on [specific contribution]. My role was [accurate description].\'94\
\'93This result was collective. In particular, [name] identified the risk, [name] developed the solution, and [name] carried the implementation.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Repairing harm\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93My wording in that conversation was unnecessarily sharp, and I can see that it may have undermined you. I am sorry. I should have raised the issue privately and focused on the specific behaviour.\'94\
If impact is uncertain:\
\'93I am concerned that my approach may have put you in a difficult position. I would like to understand the impact, if you are comfortable telling me. I will listen without debating your experience.\'94\
A good repair should not pressure the other person to reassure or forgive you. If appropriate, add a specific change:\
\'93Next time, I will discuss the concern privately and give you the relevant context before a decision is announced.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Responding ethically to conflict\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \'93I want to separate the facts, the impact, and our interpretations. Let\'92s identify what we agree happened, what remains disputed, and what process would be fair.\'94\
When you have more power:\
\'93Because I have decision-making authority here, I want to make sure disagreement is safe. Please identify any risk, conflict of interest, or missing perspective you think I should consider.\'94\
When conflict involves policy or serious conduct:\
\'93This may require a formal and impartial process. I will preserve confidentiality, avoid investigating it informally, and use the appropriate support channel.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

